e  magic question mark things like magical  beasts do exist and they are common  knowledge so do various superhuman  abilities some of which have never been  explained by men for example killer's  ability to grow claws out of nowhere i  mean maybe it could be an unconscious  use of enhancement but sure that's fine  i'm willing to accept that killer just  has a superhuman ability there but then  you have a scenario where  thousands and thousands of people flock  to see a battle between superhumans  using primarily but not always  invisible powers and are you trying to  tell me that not one of these people is  curious to know how they are able to  perform these feats  that is the very best case scenario just  a general acceptance that there are  superhumans in the world but even then  with that knowledge wouldn't you  you know maybe i don't know want to  study them  figure out how these powers emerge  whether or not you could isolate certain  genes or practices that led to them  no no one no like government agency or  extraordinarily wealthy kingdom no one's  interested in superpowers and how they  could benefit them in fact as an example  of that we can take a look at the  khaking empire this is one of the  wealthiest nations on the planet capable  of comfortably coughing up the cash for  an expedition to the dark continent  their royal family is beyond wealthy and  also very much beyond the law they have  access to anything they so desire and  yet almost none of them have any  knowledge of net you know that thing  that they can watch on tv at any given  time and also that thing that is known  by a lot of their underlings as well by  the way it always strikes me as a bit  strange to think that fourth prince  ryannick's entire mafia family and end  users and he had no idea it even existed  until now and i don't know i think i  just find it pretty hard to believe that  you can keep that knowledge of nen from  the richest and most well-connected  people on the planet ye